  "chapter": {
    "number": 65,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(66) For the end, a Song of Psalm of resurrection."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Shout to God, all the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O sing praises to his name; give glory to his praise.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Say to God, How awful are your works! through the greatness of your power your enemies shall lie to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let all the earth worship you, and sing to you; let them sing to your name. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Come and behold the works of God; he is terrible in his counsels beyond the children of men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who turns the sea into dry land; they shall go through the river on foot; there shall we rejoice in him,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who by his power",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 116
          },
          {
            "text": "is Lord over the age, his eyes look upon the nations; let not them that provoke him be exalted in themselves. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Bless our God, you⌃ Gentiles, and make the voice of his praise to be heard;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who quickens my soul in life, and does not suffer my feet to be moved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you, O God, has proved us; you have tried us with fire as silver is tried.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You brought us into the snare; you laid afflictions on our back.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You did mount men upon our heads; we went through the fire and water; but you brought us out into a place of refreshment.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will go into your house with whole burnt offerings; I will pay you my vows,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "which my lips framed, and my mouth uttered in my affliction.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will offer to you whole burnt sacrifices full of marrow, with incense and rams; I will sacrifice to you oxen with goats. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Come, hear, and I will tell, all you⌃ that fear God, how great things he has done for my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I cried to him with my mouth, and exalted him with my tongue.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If I have regarded iniquity in my heart, let not the Lord listen to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore God has listened to me; he has attended to the voice of my prayer.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed be God, who has not turned away my prayer, nor his mercy from me.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 116,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, has dominion for ever.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 65,
          "verse": 7
        }
      }
    ]
  },
